notes: >-
  Re-run against the epic's new tip after the e2e flake fix. Round 1 was six
  isolated finders over the whole range, one adversarial verifier per candidate:
  8 candidates, 1 verified. That one was fixed in 920ed10 - a trailing
  backward-looking sentence in the new guardrail comment, the only "used to" in
  the tree, saying nothing the mechanism sentence above it had not already said.
  Round 2 re-swept the fixed tip and verified nothing new. The seven refuted:
  three spec-file duplication claims (shellIsUp, the ports block, rowCount),
  refuted because the base already carries them byte-identical and the diff
  shrinks each copy rather than adding a pattern; a pub-vs-pub(crate) claim on
  e2e_core_address::init, refuted because the module is private so the item
  exports nothing either way; a Store::page lock-hold claim, refuted because
  page is new and strictly bounded where the pre-existing list it sits beside
  walks the whole ring unbounded, and docs/architecture.html specifies the
  synchronous mutex; and two design claims against the spinner artifact - a
  familiar-idioms binds="screen" over-answering claim, refuted because binds is
  scope-of-blame not scope-of-mention, and a motion-informs escalation claim,
  refuted because DEC-41 is exactly the escalation it said was missing. The
  duplication claim was raised twice by independent finders and refuted once on
  evidence from the base tree; round 2 raised it a third time and it is counted
  there, not re-verified. Round 2's correctness finder went further than
  refuting: it traced @wdio/cli's own source to prove the launcher awaits
  onPrepare before the service hook spawns the app, so the exported address is
  in the environment by then; it confirmed api.ts resolves the injected global
  ahead of the SSE bind; and it checked the one thing removing every reload
  could have broken - the per-describe state reset flows.spec used to get free -
  finding the detail panel keyed on the selected id, so the barrier each block
  waits on still holds without a navigation.
  The caller scoped this run to code: docs/ prose was not judged.
